{"id":"word:hebrew:H5329","type":"word","title":"נָצַח","subtitle":"H5329 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, to glitter from afar , i.e. to be eminent (as a superintendent, especially of the Temple services and its music); to be permanent","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָצַח (H5329) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 65 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָצַח (nâtsach) means properly, to glitter from afar , i.e. to be eminent (as a superintendent, especially of the Temple services and its music); to be permanent First listed occurrence: 1Chr 15 21."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָצַח","transliteration":"nâtsach","pronunciation":"naw-tsakh'","strong":"H5329","lemmaId":"hebrew:H5329","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["לַ/מְנַצֵּ֥חַ","לַ/מְנַצֵּ֗חַ","לַ/מְנַצֵּ֬חַ","לַ֭/מְנַצֵּחַ","לַ/מְנַצֵּ֣חַ"],"morphs":[["HRd/Vprmsa",56],["HR/Vpc",5],["HC/Vprmpa",2],["HVprmpa",1],["HVNsfsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, to glitter from afar , i.e. to be eminent (as a superintendent, especially of the Temple services and its music); to be permanent","usage":"excel, chief musician (singer), oversee(-r), set forward.","full":"H5329. natsach I. [ נָצַח ] verb be pre-eminent, enduring (Ecclus [Pi`el] make brilliant Ecclesiasticus 43:5; Ecclesiasticus 43:13 [?] (compare Oxford ed. xxxiii ); Late Hebrew נָצַח conquer , etc.; Phoenician נצח , Aramaic נְצַח , shine, be illustrious, pre-eminent, victorious ; Arabic be pure, reliable ; Ethiopic be pure, innocent ; both classes of meaning probably derived form shine, be bright, brilliant , see also Dr 1Sam 15:29 ); — Niph`al Participle active feminine נִצַּ֫חַת Jer 8:5 enduring ( מְשֻׁבָה apostasy ). Piel = act as overseer, superintendent, director , only Chronicles and Psalm-titles; &#8212; Infinitive לְנַצֵּחַ 1Chr 15:21 4 t.; participle לַמְנַצֵּחַ Hab 3:19 ; Psa 4:1 54t. Psalms; plural מְנַצְּחִים 2Chr 2:1 ; 2:17 ; 34:13 ; — 1 in building temple 2Chr 2:1 ; 2:17 ; Ezra 3:8-9 , compare 2Chr 34:12-13 ,. 2 in ministry of house of ׳י 1Chr 23:4 . 3 in liturgical service of song, עלהֿשׁמינית , over the bass voices, leading them with כִּנֹּרוֺת 1Chr 15:21 ; לַמְנַצֵּחַ in titles Psalms has probably simile meaning, = musical director or choirmaster ; Greek Vrss. of 2nd cent. A.D., Aq Theod Sym, and so Jerome, think of Aramaic victorious , but no clear explanation; ᵐ5 εἰς τὸ τέλος (probably לַמִּנְצָח ) follows ordinary meaning of noun נֵצַח , which may be explained in eschatological sense as referring to end of age of world after Euseb Theod; or for full rendering after De; neither satisfactory. Chronicles, near in date, gives the clue which is intrinsically probably: לְ indicates, not assignment (nothing special in these Psalms to suggest it, and assignment of Psalms for such use a matter of course), but that these Psalms were taken by final editor from an older major Psalter known as the Director's Collection, compare the still earlier collections known as קרח (ל)בני (ל)אסף, (ל)דוד, . The 55 Psalms with למנצח were taken 39 from Davidic, 9 from Korahite, and 5 from Asaphic Psalters; only 2anonymous. Habakkuk 3 originally belonged to Director's Psalter. This and other Director's Psalms have musical directions in titles. The Director's Psalter was probably the prayer-book of synagogue of Greek period, presupposed by our Hab., the collection of the twelve Minor Prophets, the prophetic canon, and Daniel (see Br Gen. Intr. 123 ). [ נְצַח ] verb Hithpa. distinguish oneself (see Biblical Hebrew I. נצח ); — Participle מִתְנַצַּח Dan 6:4 , עַל person","rootNote":"a primitive root; also as denominative from 5331","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 15 21","keyReferences":["1Chr 15 21","1Chr 23 4","2Chr 2 1","2Chr 2 17","2Chr 34 12","2Chr 34 13","Ezra 3 8","Ezra 3 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":65,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 15 21","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/נַצֵּֽחַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"1Chr 23 4","book":"1Chr","chapter":23,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/נַצֵּ֨חַ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"2Chr 2 1","book":"2Chr","chapter":2,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/מְנַצְּחִ֣ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vprmpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 2 17","book":"2Chr","chapter":2,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"מְנַצְּחִ֖ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVprmpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 34 12","book":"2Chr","chapter":34,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/נַצֵּ֑חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"2Chr 34 13","book":"2Chr","chapter":34,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּֽ/מְנַצְּחִים֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vprmpa"},{"reference":"Ezra 3 8","book":"Ezra","chapter":3,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/נַצֵּ֖חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"Ezra 3 9","book":"Ezra","chapter":3,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/נַצֵּ֛חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"Hab 3 19","book":"Hab","chapter":3,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/מְנַצֵּ֖חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Vprmsa"},{"reference":"Jer 8 5","book":"Jer","chapter":8,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נִצַּ֑חַת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVNsfsa"},{"reference":"Ps 4 1","book":"Ps","chapter":4,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/מְנַצֵּ֥חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Vprmsa"},{"reference":"Ps 5 1","book":"Ps","chapter":5,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/מְנַצֵּ֥חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Vprmsa"},{"reference":"Ps 6 1","book":"Ps","chapter":6,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/מְנַצֵּ֣חַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Vprmsa"},{"reference":"Ps 8 1","book":"Ps","chapter":8,"